WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:32.041
<b>Here Lord Krishna tells Arjuna</b>

2
00:00:32.041 --> 00:00:34.625
<b>that he should perform actions (Karma).</b>

3
00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:38.000
<b>Action (Karma) is always superior to inaction,</b>

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.208
<b>and even the basic necessities of the human body</b>

5
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:43.708
<b>cannot be fulfilled without action (Karma).</b>

6
00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:51.291
<b>In the previous few verses Lord Krishna stated,</b>

7
00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:53.708
<b>that remaining inactive is not right.</b>

8
00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:56.625
<b>It is better to perform actions</b>
<b>than to renounce actions,</b>

9
00:00:56.625 --> 00:01:01.125
<b>and it is best to perform actions </b>
<b>without attachment to the fruits.</b>

10
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:03.583
<b>This is selfless Karma Yoga </b>
<b>(Nishkam Karma Yoga),</b>

11
00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>which purifies a person's mind.</b>

12
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.583
<b>Therefore, Arjuna should perform actions.</b>

13
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:17.375
<b>Understand the point made here about</b>
<b>the basic necessities of the body</b>

14
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:20.875
<b>- every person, according </b>
<b>to their natural qualities,</b>

15
00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:22.791
<b>according to their tendencies,</b>

16
00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:25.583
<b>has to perform various activities</b>

17
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:30.458
<b>These activities help sustain their body.</b>

18
00:01:30.458 --> 00:01:31.750
<b>For example,</b>

19
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:36.208
<b>a Brahmin begs for his livelihood.</b>

20
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:40.208
<b>This is sufficient according to his physical needs.</b>

21
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:41.041
<b>But</b>

22
00:01:41.041 --> 00:01:44.250
<b>a Kshatriya is not allowed to beg,</b>

23
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.041
<b>because the duty of a Kshatriya is to fight,</b>

24
00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:52.625
<b>for which it is extremely important</b>
<b>for the body to be strong,</b>

25
00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:57.791
<b>and for this very reason regular food and </b>
<b>special diet are also necessary,</b>

26
00:01:57.791 --> 00:02:01.291
<b>which is not possible from the </b>
<b>food received in begging.</b>

27
00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:02.708
<b>The conclusion is that</b>

28
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.583
<b>for a warrior like Arjuna,</b>

29
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:08.500
<b>neither is it appropriate to renounce action,</b>

30
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.958
<b>nor to think of going to the forest and begging.</b>

31
00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:15.458
<b>If he wants purification of the mind,</b>

32
00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:18.666
<b>then his path will only pass through action.</b>

33
00:02:18.666 --> 00:02:21.583
<b>For Arjuna, fighting is the right thing,</b>

34
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:25.458
<b>whether it is viewed from a logical perspective</b>

35
00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:27.791
<b>or a spiritual perspective.</b>

36
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:36.000
<b>Everyone has some responsibilities,</b>

37
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.500
<b>some duties in life.</b>

38
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.833
<b>Many times a person fulfills these </b>
<b>responsibilities with enthusiasm,</b>

39
00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:47.916
<b>but many times one does not </b>
<b>feel like performing duties at all.</b>

40
00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:52.000
<b>A state of mind to abandon responsibility arises.</b>

41
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.500
<b>Here, if there is a need for momentary rest, </b>
<b>it can certainly be taken.</b>

42
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:05.541
<b>This will give the body and mind </b>
<b>the energy to re-engage in action.</b>

43
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:08.750
<b>But if this is not the case,</b>

44
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:18.250
<b>then is it right to be a slave to a weak state of </b>
<b>mind, to leave the duty incomplete, to abandon it? </b>

45
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.916
<b>No.</b>

46
00:03:19.916 --> 00:03:23.333
<b>It is not right to run away from duty.</b>

47
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:28.291
<b>Try to remove yourself from this situation and see</b>

48
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.583
<b>- and think</b>

49
00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:34.416
<b>- which person is better?</b>

50
00:03:34.416 --> 00:03:42.250
<b>The one who, as soon as the mind becomes weak, </b>
<b>abandons duty and runs away in the middle?</b>

51
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.916
<b>Or the one who never backs </b>
<b>down from his responsibility.</b>

52
00:03:47.916 --> 00:03:50.083
<b>Always fulfills it.</b>

53
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:52.250
<b>You also know</b>

54
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.083
<b>that never run away from duty.</b>

55
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:58.833
<b>This is right.</b>

56
00:03:58.833 --> 00:04:03.333
<b>It also shows respect for others.</b>

57
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.458
<b>Man is not alone,</b>

58
00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:09.750
<b>his every responsibility is </b>
<b>connected with someone else.</b>

59
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.708
<b>The responsibility of parents </b>
<b>is connected with children,</b>

60
00:04:12.708 --> 00:04:15.666
<b>the responsibility of a friend with a friend,</b>

61
00:04:15.666 --> 00:04:19.166
<b>professional responsibility is </b>
<b>connected with colleagues.</b>

62
00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:21.500
<b>Running away from one's responsibility</b>

63
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.750
<b>is also disrespecting others.</b>

64
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.416
<b>Stay dutiful.</b>

65
00:04:27.416 --> 00:04:30.041
<b>Overcome the weakness of the mind,</b>

66
00:04:30.041 --> 00:04:35.875
<b>never abandon responsibility </b>
<b>by falling for its talks.</b>

67
00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:44.708
<b>Emotions are an integral part of human life,</b>

68
00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:46.708
<b>they are necessary.</b>

69
00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:47.875
<b>But</b>

70
00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:51.541
<b>being overly emotional is also not right,</b>

71
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:56.791
<b>especially when it interferes with your duty.</b>

72
00:04:56.791 --> 00:04:58.958
<b>For example</b>

73
00:04:58.958 --> 00:05:00.666
<b>- there are many such families,</b>

74
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:03.416
<b>some of whom you also know,</b>

75
00:05:03.416 --> 00:05:08.625
<b>where parents become so</b>
<b>emotional towards their children</b>

76
00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:16.041
<b>that they cannot see them suffering any pain. </b>
<b>They fulfill their every little desire,</b>

77
00:05:16.041 --> 00:05:19.958
<b>keep them away from every difficulty.</b>

78
00:05:19.958 --> 00:05:21.125
<b>For this reason</b>

79
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:24.416
<b>many children also become very stubborn.</b>

80
00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:27.875
<b>They are only learning to do as they please,</b>

81
00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:33.333
<b>and they run away from whatever </b>
<b>does not please their mind.</b>

82
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:38.458
<b>Parents also, being emotional, let this go on.</b>

83
00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:43.750
<b>They ignore the small stubbornness</b>
<b>of the children.</b>

84
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.375
<b>But</b>

85
00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:48.875
<b>the problem is not the </b>
<b>small stubbornness of the children,</b>

86
00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:55.583
<b>the problem is that if this </b>
<b>slowly becomes their nature,</b>

87
00:05:55.583 --> 00:05:59.166
<b>then life will be very difficult.</b>

88
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:04.125
<b>The child will not always be able to </b>
<b>stay under the umbrella of parents.</b>

89
00:06:04.125 --> 00:06:05.375
<b>For higher education,</b>

90
00:06:05.375 --> 00:06:06.416
<b>livelihood</b>

91
00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>and many other reasons, one will have </b>
<b>to go out into the society,</b>

92
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:12.958
<b>face difficult situations,</b>

93
00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:17.291
<b>encounter different types of people.</b>

94
00:06:17.291 --> 00:06:23.583
<b>If they have always been kept in </b>
<b>a very secure environment,</b>

95
00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:27.458
<b>then all this will be overwhelming for them.</b>

96
00:06:27.458 --> 00:06:30.583
<b>They will feel directionless.</b>

97
00:06:30.583 --> 00:06:32.416
<b>Just being emotional</b>

98
00:06:32.416 --> 00:06:37.166
<b>and keeping the child away from </b>
<b>every little suffering is not right.</b>

99
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:40.708
<b>For their happy future, it is necessary</b>

100
00:06:40.708 --> 00:06:44.000
<b>that they also see some difficulties,</b>

101
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.291
<b>are taught the lesson of performing duties,</b>

102
00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:50.500
<b>are made to understand the </b>
<b>importance of responsibility.</b>

103
00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.875
<b>And the parents have to do this.</b>

104
00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:55.916
<b>This is their duty.</b>

105
00:07:00.583 --> 00:07:06.083
<b>In our professional life, it is natural to</b>
<b>face difficult situations,</b>

106
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:08.041
<b>some complex work,</b>

107
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:10.375
<b>some difficult colleague,</b>

108
00:07:10.375 --> 00:07:15.416
<b>or some responsibility that seems impossible.</b>

109
00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:21.125
<b>Many times a person tries to </b>
<b>run away from all this.</b>

110
00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:22.791
<b>He tries</b>

111
00:07:22.791 --> 00:07:25.750
<b>that someone else should do his work,</b>

112
00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.416
<b>or</b>

113
00:07:27.416 --> 00:07:29.583
<b>he himself quits this job.</b>

114
00:07:29.583 --> 00:07:30.708
<b>But</b>

115
00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:32.583
<b>- the truth is</b>

116
00:07:32.583 --> 00:07:37.666
<b>that this will not solve the problem.</b>

117
00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:41.500
<b>Difficult situations will still come.</b>

118
00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.041
<b>Then what should be done?</b>

119
00:07:44.041 --> 00:07:46.916
<b>Learn to face the situations.</b>

120
00:07:46.916 --> 00:07:49.291
<b>Focus on these two things</b>

121
00:07:49.291 --> 00:07:50.708
<b>- First</b>

122
00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:56.416
<b>- don't pass your responsibility on to others </b>
<b>- complete it.</b>

123
00:07:56.416 --> 00:07:58.166
<b>Think,</b>

124
00:07:58.166 --> 00:08:03.916
<b>if someone else can do this work, </b>
<b>then why can't you?</b>

125
00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:11.208
<b>Try to learn how someone </b>
<b>else would solve this situation.</b>

126
00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:13.666
<b>Take help from someone.</b>

127
00:08:13.666 --> 00:08:16.750
<b>This will not only solve the problem,</b>

128
00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:20.583
<b>but your work efficiency will also increase.</b>

129
00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:21.708
<b>Second</b>

130
00:08:21.708 --> 00:08:24.000
<b>- stay positive.</b>

131
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.375
<b>No situation is completely bad,</b>

132
00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:31.708
<b>it also has many good aspects.</b>

133
00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:32.791
<b>For example</b>

134
00:08:32.791 --> 00:08:37.500
<b>- this very work of yours provides </b>
<b>you with the means of life,</b>

135
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:41.250
<b>keeps your family happy.</b>

136
00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.583
<b>This is also an important aspect.</b>

137
00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:46.375
<b>And also,</b>

138
00:08:46.375 --> 00:08:52.083
<b>remember those past incidents </b>
<b>when you were stuck in some difficulty,</b>

139
00:08:52.083 --> 00:08:53.666
<b>were scared,</b>

140
00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:54.416
<b>but</b>

141
00:08:54.416 --> 00:08:58.416
<b>with time that difficulty passed.</b>

142
00:08:58.416 --> 00:08:59.916
<b>Remember</b>

143
00:08:59.916 --> 00:09:02.291
<b>- no difficulty is permanent,</b>

144
00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:03.541
<b>it will pass.</b>

145
00:09:03.541 --> 00:09:06.916
<b>There is only one way to progress,</b>

146
00:09:06.916 --> 00:09:08.208
<b>and that is</b>

147
00:09:08.208 --> 00:09:10.916
<b>to fulfill one's duty.</b>

148
00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:15.666
<b>It is not right to run away from </b>
<b>it under any circumstances.</b>

